course: dictionary
lesson: 14609
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and Pomeranian is one of them. Read the words around it to find the right one. «Mia brushed her Pomeranian every morning.» The brushing tells you it is an animal, and the most likely animal is a dog.
explain: Pomeranian can also name a person. «Pomeranian sailors sailed across the Baltic Sea.» The sea and the sailors are the clues. Here it means a person from Pomerania, a region by the sea.
explain: As an adjective, Pomeranian describes something from Pomerania. «The Pomeranian coast has sandy beaches.» Ask: is the word naming a thing or describing one? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Pomeranian can be a noun and an adjective, so it can name a thing or describe one.
fact: As a dog, a Pomeranian is a very small, fluffy dog with a fox-like face, pointed ears and a thick coat.
fact: Pomeranians are often orange or cream, and people often shorten the name to «Pom».
fact: Pomerania is a region by the Baltic Sea, now in Poland and Germany.
fact: A person from Pomerania is also called a Pomeranian, and so is a thing that comes from Pomerania.
exercise: «Mia's Pomeranian puppy yapped at the postman.» What is a Pomeranian in this sentence? | A kind of cold weather | *A small, fluffy dog | A tall tree in a park | A boat that sails on the sea
exercise: «The Pomeranian coast has sandy beaches by the Baltic Sea.» What does Pomeranian describe here? | *Coming from Pomerania | A very small thing | A fluffy and orange colour | Something that yaps at strangers
exercise: Which short name is often used for a Pomeranian dog? | Pam | *Pom | Pen | Pop
test: «The Pomeranian people of the region had their own customs.» What does Pomeranian mean here? | A tall castle on a hill | A cold, grey wind | *People from Pomerania, the region by the Baltic Sea | A small, fluffy dog
test: «The pampered Pomeranian yapped at every stranger who came near.» What does yapped suggest? | Ran away quietly | Slept all day | Sang a happy song | *Barked in short, sharp bursts
exam: Mila says, «Pomeranian can only mean a dog.» Is she right? | Yes, but only in history lessons | Yes, it never means anything else | *No, it can also name a person from Pomerania | No, it means a boat
